"[2511.14116] FailSafe: High-performance Resilient Serving (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.14116)\nciteturn2393view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.14116\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 160\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 18 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:FailSafe: High-performance Resilient Serving\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Ziyi Xu , cite6†Zhiqiang Xie , cite7†Swapnil Gandhi , cite8†Christos Kozyrakis L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled FailSafe: High-performance Resilient Serving, by Ziyi Xu and 3 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite9†View PDF cite10†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Tensor parallelism (TP) enables large language models (LLMs) to scale inference efficiently across multiple GPUs, but its tight coupling makes systems fragile: a single GPU failure can halt execution, trigger costly KVCache recomputation, and introduce long-term compute and memory imbalance. We present FailSafe, a fault-tolerant TP serving system that sustains high performance under irregular GPU availability.\nL17: FailSafe introduces three techniques to balance computation and memory across GPUs: (1) Cyclic KVCache Placement for uniform memory utilization, (2) Hybrid Attention combining tensor- and data-parallel attention to eliminate stragglers, and (3) Fine-Grained Load-Aware Routing to dynamically balance requests. It further employs proactive KVCache backup and on-demand weight recovery to avoid expensive recomputation and redundant data transfers.\nL18: We implement these techniques in a lightweight serving engine compatible with existing LLM infrastructures. Evaluated on an 8xH100 DGX system with real-world fault traces and representative workloads, FailSafe achieves up to 2x higher throughput and two orders of magnitude lower recovery latency compared to standard fault handling approaches.\nL19: Even with up to three GPU failures, FailSafe sustains high throughput and balanced utilization, demonstrating robust and efficient LLM serving under dynamic and unreliable hardware conditions.\nL20: Subjects:  | Distributed, Parallel, and Cluster Computing (cs.DC)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite11†arXiv:2511.14116 [cs.DC]\nL22:    | (or cite12†arXiv:2511.14116v1 [cs.DC] for this version)\nL23:    | cite13†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.14116†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Ziyi Xu [cite14†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Tue, 18 Nov 2025 04:01:46 UTC (10,560 KB)\nL28: \nL29: Full-text links:\nL30: \nL31: ## Access Paper:\nL32: \nL33: View a PDF of the paper titled FailSafe: High-performance Resilient Serving, by Ziyi Xu and 3 other authors\nL34: \nL35:   * cite9†View PDF L36:   * cite10†HTML (experimental) L37:   * cite15†TeX Source L38: \nL39: cite16†view license†creativecommons.org L40: \nL41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: cs.DC\nL44: \nL45: cite17†< prev |   cite18†next > L46: \nL47: cite19†new | cite20†recent | cite21†2025-11 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite22†cs L52: ### References & Citations\nL53: \nL54:   * cite23†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L55:   * cite24†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L56:   * cite25†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L57: \nL58: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL59: \nL60: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL61: \nL62: [Button: ×]\nL63: \nL64: loading...\nL65: \nL66: Data provided by:\nL67: \nL68: ### Bookmark\nL69: \nL70: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL71: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL72: \nL73: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL74: \nL75: Bibliographic Explorer (cit