ian Ichter , cite29†Szymon Jakubczak , cite30†Rowan Jen , cite31†Tim Jones , cite32†Ben Katz , cite33†Liyiming Ke , cite34†Chandra Kuchi , cite35†Marinda Lamb , cite36†Devin LeBlanc , cite37†Sergey Levine , cite38†Adrian Li-Bell , cite39†Yao Lu , cite40†Vishnu Mano , cite41†Mohith Mothukuri , cite42†Suraj Nair , cite43†Karl Pertsch , cite44†Allen Z.\nL11: Ren , cite45†Charvi Sharma , cite46†Lucy Xiaoyang Shi , cite47†Laura Smith , cite48†Jost Tobias Springenberg , cite49†Kyle Stachowicz , cite50†Will Stoeckle , cite51†Alex Swerdlow , cite52†James Tanner , cite53†Marcel Torne , cite54†Quan Vuong , cite55†Anna Walling , cite56†Haohuan Wang , cite57†Blake Williams , cite58†Sukwon Yoo , cite59†Lili Yu , cite60†Ury Zhilinsky , cite61†Zhiyuan Zhou L12: View a PDF of the paper titled $\\pi^{*}_{0.6}$: a VLA That Learns From Experience, by Physical Intelligence and 55 other authors\nL13: \nL14: cite62†View PDF cite63†HTML (experimental) L15: > Abstract:We study how vision-language-action (VLA) models can improve through real-world deployments via reinforcement learning (RL). We present a general-purpose method, RL with Experience and Corrections via Advantage-conditioned Policies (RECAP), that provides for RL training of VLAs via advantage conditioning.\nL16: Our method incorporates heterogeneous data into the self-improvement process, including demonstrations, data from on-policy collection, and expert teleoperated interventions provided during autonomous execution. RECAP starts by pre-training a generalist VLA with offline RL, which we call $\\pi^{*}_{0.6}$, that can then be specialized to attain high performance on downstream tasks through on-robot data collection.\nL17: We show that the $\\pi^{*}_{0.6}$ model trained with the full RECAP method can fold laundry in real homes, reliably assemble boxes, and make espresso drinks using a professional espresso machine. On some of the hardest tasks, RECAP more than doubles task throughput and roughly halves the task failure rate.\nL18: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG); Robotics (cs.RO)\nL19: Cite as:  | cite64†arXiv:2511.14759 [cs.LG]\nL20:    | (or cite65†arXiv:2511.14759v2 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL21:    | cite66†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.14759†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Brian Ichter [cite67†view email ]\nL25: cite5†[v1] Tue, 18 Nov 2025 18:58:55 UTC (22,750 KB)\nL26: [v2] Wed, 19 Nov 2025 04:34:49 UTC (22,750 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled $\\pi^{*}_{0.6}$: a VLA That Learns From Experience, by Physical Intelligence and 55 other authors\nL33: \nL34:   * cite62†View PDF L35:   * cite63†HTML (experimental) L36:   * cite68†TeX Source L37: \nL38: cite69†view license L39: ### Current browse context:\nL40: \nL41: cs.LG\nL42: \nL43: cite70†< prev |   cite71†next > L44: \nL45: cite72†new | cite73†recent | cite74†2025-11 L46: \nL47: Change to browse by:\nL48: \nL49: cite75†cs L50: cite76†cs.RO L51: \nL52: ### References & Citations\nL53: \nL54:   * cite77†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L55:   * cite78†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L56:   * cite79†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L57: \nL58: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL59: \nL60: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL61: \nL62: [Button: ×]\nL63: \nL64: loading...\nL65: \nL66: Data provided by:\nL67: \nL68: ### Bookmark\nL69: \nL70: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL71: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL72: \nL73: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL74: \nL75: Bibliographic Explorer (cite80†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL76: \nL77: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL78: \nL79: Connected Papers (cite81†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com )\nL80: \nL81: [Input] Litmaps Toggle\nL82: \n